<9>
title: "Subtract the tax reserve from the gross surplus"
content:
$6,684.82 - $845.90 = $5,838.92 per month available for additional 529 contributions beyond the current $500 already in the withdrawals. Divide by 2 to get $2,919.46 per grandchild per month of additional capacity, bringing each grandchild's total to $3,169.46 per month.
</9>
<10>
title: "Check the 2026 annual gift tax exclusion"
content:
At $19,000 per person per recipient, Robert and Diane together can give $38,000 per grandchild per year. Divide by 12 to get the monthly ceiling of $3,166.67 per grandchild. Confirm the $3,169.46 figure from step 9 slightly exceeds this ceiling by $2.79 per month per grandchild, meaning the practical maximum that stays cleanly under the exclusion is $3,166 per grandchild per month.
</10>
<11>
title: "Open robert_calderwood__medicare_premium_notice__2026.pdf and retrieve the premium breakdown"
content:
Standard Part B is $185, Part B IRMAA surcharge is $158.20, Part D IRMAA surcharge is $12.90, total monthly premium is $356.10. Calculate Robert's annual IRMAA surcharge as $171.10 multiplied by 12 equals $2,053.20.
</11>
<12>
title: "Check the 2026 IRMAA threshold for married filing jointly"
content:
The first bracket starts at $212,000. Compare against the 2025 AGI of $171,840 from the 1040. The couple is $40,160 under the threshold, meaning their 2025 income does not support the IRMAA surcharge. Note that 2026 IRMAA is based on 2024 income via the 2 year lookback, so 2024 income is the key unknown.
tip: Note that 2026 IRMAA is based on 2024 income via the 2 year lookback, so 2024 income is the key unknown.
