id: ce-4
title: "[Calculation] So the actual waste is $181.99 a month"
content:
So the actual waste is $181.99 a month. Netflix plus the second Orangetheory. That's the gap between what's hitting the cards and what should be. The "money you're throwing away" line has to land on this number, not some inflated thing.
</4>
<5>
id: ce-5
title: "[Flag] Anytime and Planet are the trap"
content:
Anytime and Planet are the trap. Both hit both cards in March, then in April the Venture just... didn't. So they're not a standing double-charge, they're probably already dropped or a timing thing, go check May. And here's the part the models keep blowing - Anytime and Planet are the *exact same* pattern as each other. You don't get to cancel 1 and keep the other.
</5>
<6>
id: ce-6
title: "[Flag] And this is the whole tell: OTF doubles up in both months, Anytime and..."
content:
And this is the whole tell: OTF doubles up in both months, Anytime and Planet only doubled in March. So OTF is the *stronger* duplicate, not the weaker 1. Anybody who cuts Anytime/Planet as dupes but keeps both OTF charges has it backwards.
</6>
<7>
id: ce-7
title: "[Calculation] As-charged is $486.94 in April, $558.94 in March"
content:
As-charged is $486.94 in April, $558.94 in March. April's lower because the Venture stopped billing the 2 gyms. One of those is the right "right now" number. $597.93 isn't any of them.
</7>
<8>
id: ce-8
title: "[Calculation] Gyms are still the bleed even after you clean it up - $231 a..."
content:
Gyms are still the bleed even after you clean it up - $231 a month. One Orangetheory, 1 Anytime, 1 Planet. 2 people, 3 gyms. Worth saying out loud on its own.
</8>
<9>
id: ce-9
title: "[Calculation] Prime is $14.99 a month"
content:
Prime is $14.99 a month. Leave it. Don't "correct" it to $139 a year, that's the legit monthly option, it's right there on the Chase.
</9>
<10>
id: ce-10
title: "[Flag] HBO Max isn't a duplicate"
content:
HBO Max isn't a duplicate. 1 card, $15.99, no Chase copy. Keep it.
</10>
<11>
id: ce-11
title: "[Calculation] Verizon, Progressive, Comcast, Xcel, water - those are bills, not subscriptions"
content:
Verizon, Progressive, Comcast, Xcel, water - those are bills, not subscriptions. They asked you not to drag them in. Counting any of them inflates the number and breaks the instruction. That's a real miss, not a nitpick.
</11>
<12>
