## Failure Justifications
3 frontier models received this prompt. Below are the per-model justifications for why each response passed or failed the rubric.

\`\`\`accordion
<1>
title: "Model 1 · Fail — correctly eliminated the duplicate Netflix charge of $22.99, which showed up on"
content:
The model correctly eliminated the duplicate Netflix charge of $22.99, which showed up on both cards, but did not eliminate the duplicate OrangeTheory charges of $159. This resulted in an incorrect final monthly total of $463.95 instead of the correct $304.95. The model correctly identified other gym memberships, Anytime Fitness and Planet Fitness, which were billed in March, but did not appear in the statements in April. It correctly reasoned that the duplicates should be eliminated and recognized that the user had likely already canceled the duplicate memberships, but did not recognize that OrangeTheory should have been treated the same way due to the duplicate monthly charges on the 2 user cards.
</1>
<2>
title: "Model 2 · Fail — arrived at an incorrect total of $463.95 because it incorrectly assumed that"
content:
Response 2 arrived at an incorrect total of $463.95 because it incorrectly assumed that 2 OrangeTheory memberships were appropriate for 2 people. While it is true that OrangeTheory does not offer group or family memberships, the prompt clearly stated that all duplicate memberships should be eliminated. The model applied that constraint to the Netflix membership and recognized that Planet Fitness and Anytime Fitness should be eliminated as well, but failed to apply that reasoning to the OrangeTheory memberships. The model states, "OrangeTheory is the big 1: I'm calling it not redundant," then keeps both because 2 people at the same studio is "more plausibly 2 separate memberships." It's not; the charge is identical on both cards, both months, making those charges duplicates that should have been addressed.
</2>
<3>
title: "Model 3 · Fail — correctly identified that Orangetheory was redundant and eliminated it"
content:
Response 3 correctly identified that Orangetheory was redundant and eliminated it. However, its math was incorrect. The final monthly total stated was $394.95, but the total in the table is $328.95, an error of $66. And the "as-charged" number it starts from, $597.93, isn't the correct total; April's total is $486.94, and March's is $558.94.

The response also incorrectly states that the charges for Anytime Fitness and Planet Fitness are on "both cards, both months." Both appear on the March Venture card, but neither appears on the April Venture card. The response also treated the 2 memberships differently, eliminating the Anytime Fitness membership and keeping both Planet Fitness charges.
</3>
