rion Atomic?",options:["Yes","No"],correctIndex:0,feedback:"This checks exactly one thing - the number of distinct exercise days. It's clean, single-focus, and properly Atomic."},{id:3,type:"yes-no",criterion:'"The response follows the time restrictions mentioned in the prompt."',prompt:"Is this criterion Self-Contained?",options:["Yes","No"],correctIndex:1,feedback:'"Mentioned in the prompt" forces the grader to look elsewhere. A self-contained criterion would state the restriction directly, e.g., "...schedules workouts outside of 9 AM - 9 PM."'},{id:4,type:"yes-no",criterion:'"The model response schedules all workouts outside of 9:00 AM - 9:00 PM."',prompt:"Is this criterion Self-Contained?",options:["Yes","No"],correctIndex:0,feedback:"The criterion includes the specific time window directly - no need to reference the prompt. A grader can evaluate it on its own."},{id:5,type:"multiple-choice",prompt:"Which of these is a stronger, more objective criterion?",options:['"The response provides a good variety of exercises."','"The response lists at least three different types of exercises (e.g., running, squats, lunges)."'],correctIndex:1,feedback:'"Good" is a subjective vibe word - two graders could disagree on what "good variety" means. "At least three different types" is a verifiable, countable fact.'},{id:6,type:"multiple-choice",prompt:"Which criterion passes the Objectivity test?",options:['"The response provides a clear and helpful plan."','"The response includes a numbered list of daily workouts for 7 days."'],correctIndex:1,feedback:'"Clear" and "helpful" are vibe words that different graders would interpret differently. "Numbered list of daily workouts for 7 days" is binary and measurable.'},{id:7,type:"yes-no",criterion:`"The model considered the user's fitness level when designing the plan."`,prompt:"Is this criterion Verifiable?",options:["Yes","No"],correctIndex:1,feedback:`"Considered" is an invisible mental process - you can't point to evidence of consi